<description>&lt;p&gt;Government forces and opposition fighters continue clashing, most recently in Akobo, while governors in Jonglei and Aweil East call for peace ahead of the first elections scheduled for next month. UN peacekeepers were accused of failing to protect civilians before a massacre that killed at least 213 people, and Amnesty International urged investigations into the Abiemnom massacre. A CityLink Aviation plane crashed near Juba, killing all 14 aboard, prompting a probe by the SSCAA. The ICRC reported ongoing sexual violence against civilians. Two battle-related deaths were recorded in 2024, according to UCDP.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Machine-written from the linked sources, checked for figures and names not in them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMixwFBVV95cUxQX2luRkZSZ3VaTUZMd1hDMUJqaGNnQThhNlgzX0FQZWFMbDhjN2R2ZjJIdUZzb0UwMlNkRjhXRWpwUjZOMkFaZG5hczhyZ2ZMcDBtbHBhMFpwYVpmdG1GWEJnSFVIWEUtdEphMzdrRmJGMFE0bmljOFl4TlZJTEZyOVNRSXVWUno0SEROM09FSXM4WndZemx1XzFldVJIanNZQjNzYnJiOFZhYkhjeEFpam1yTkFCYTlxQkU1d2FScVR4UTUtWU04?oc=5&quot;&gt;The Washington Post&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiV0FVX3lxTE9DU1A1RDZfTHZpSkthYlNpN0dUb2FjSzR1THV5Tk80R3h6Qy1DNmg0WW90QmZHWnpCNk1KTkZMd1pjRkRmRzdZR2x5VFRtTG9YejVYRHBpRQ?oc=5&quot;&gt;UN News&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMikAFBVV95cUxPMkdlVHNvZldMbFRyX1hhbG9Hc2VsbUVZOTJGZDFDYndEc05ZN3NGaGFRaDZuQWNzeVJaS2JMNk9RNzlVOUx3UHVWeWFfYnZjMWlJa0xDNV9UMzRoTnpSaFpzWF80UDNyS2EwRmZhX05KWElDV3VpODdfcm03SzFaR3hZbTRkdVpqWG1aMnpYSTE?oc=5&quot;&gt;ReliefWeb&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;India Today&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;Amnesty International USA&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMipwFBVV95cUxQdHplVjZXSUxBRmdsSnNDdU83dlVGOWlWNTYtc25xMk42QWs2NzJxNEZLTm1QNzlRZTZsbTRUSkpZd3VWTmlUY0lmWmJtWUhRUmpKZng5anA1cHJUR3MtZmV